WEBVTT

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:06.490
J-Just now... what did you say?

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:10.450
Lord Muneshige and I have had sex together.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:13.120
Did it not air in Tres España?

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:13.910
Live, even.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.200
Live?!

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.000
Since there was blood, we may have broken the code of ethics...

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:21.790
There was blood?!

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:25.210
In the end, I was the one who pierced through him...

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.590
I would dare say we did it around 50 times.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.590
F-Fifty times... Lord Muneshige.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:37.600
I will clear my husband's name.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.190
En garde!

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:46.610
Arcabuz Cruz!

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:33.090
Now that we've seen through San Martin's trick with numbers,

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:36.720
I bet they are going to switch to a more aggressive offense.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:37.430
That's why...

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.930
All ships, shift elevation angle by 15º.

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:41.720
Slowly fall back!

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:47.190
We will aim for the center of the enemy's main fleet.

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:51.030
All ships, initialize gravitational navigation!

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:54.150
It looks like they're headed for our main fleet.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:56.910
In that case... we'll change our course as well.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:01.330
We will pull around Musashi and give pursuit.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:06.330
They won't be able to run if we force them to drive through our main fleet,

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.500
making us victorious.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.760
But I won't let that happen!

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.890
First I have to stall their mechanical phoenix's aircraft carrier.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:22.310
Burn, my flames!

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:23.730
Zoom, my diabolical pitch!

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.910
Strike! Batter out!

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:41.870
Dear sister.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.580
He isn't out yet.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.130
You came prepared for this?

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.760
You didn't have to spell it out if you knew.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.390
Was that the power of money?

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.600
This is the power of money!

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:12.900
These contracts are from all our students contributing to this battlefield.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.610
The contents state that in exchange for personally paying a tenth of their salaries,

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:21.120
a tenth of the offensive power they wield in battle will go straight to me!

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.330
You put that power behind flicking a coin?

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.620
That's exactly what I did!

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.000
Don't underestimate the baseball team!

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.000
I did it!

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:40.590
I should warn you.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:43.970
I figured out the trick behind why your diabolical pitches vanish.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.350
I'll punch it next time!

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:46.890
Pedro!

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:50.850
Dear little sister, there won't be any intentional walks this game!

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:11.750
It's right here!

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:22.970
What do you think?

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:24.510
Master Noriki lost, didn't he?

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:27.010
The pitcher caught the line drive, so he's out.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:28.560
But...

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.190
Pedro, your hand!

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.650
Our diabolical pitch won!

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:38.440
Judge.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:46.370
Captain Takakane! It looks like this is it for us!

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:48.740
May our captains have good luck in battle!

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:07.850
Enemy Gods of War have commenced battle around Musashi's stern. Over.

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:10.850
What's this? Is there less chaff now?

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:18.940
Isn't that...?!

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.900
Pathfinder Byakko!

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.450
Hiro, I'm taking out Suzaku!

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:27.450
Judge!

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:33.290
The chaff is currently sparse enough for automated dolls to dispose of the rest.

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:36.500
Lady Suzu, I request that you serve as my substitute

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:39.300
and process data until we have completed that task. Over.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.340
Substitute for you? But how?

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:47.220
I will send outside information into your sensory system

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:49.890
and convert it so that you can perceive data as sound.

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:52.140
Is that acceptable? Over.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:53.310
Judge.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:56.230
Here.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:04.700
Preparations are complete. Over.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:07.280
Then here I go. Over.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.710
Is this... the world?

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:22.800
A-A clean cushion.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:31.760
Lady Suzu, you can sense data from all directions, correct? Over.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:36.270
She is perceiving almost everything perfectly within a 30km radius. Over.

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:37.850
Wow!

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.150
I'll shave off as much of the enemy fire as I can!

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:49.620
Clap!

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:54.580
<i>What else are Shinto spells for?!</i>

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:56.580
Locked on!

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:01.250
Hey!

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:02.090
It didn't go off!

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:03.800
What the hell?! That gave me a heart attack!

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.510
Isn't it great that no one got hurt?

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:09.550
What's that?

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.180
Good evening!

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.180
I am not a suspicious fellow!

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.810
I am the incubus, Ito Kenji!

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:19.230
Friendship has brought me aboard your vessel today!

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:22.940
For friendship, I, Nenji, will offer a helping hand!

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:26.650
And a one, two! One, two! Put energy into it!

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.660
I might have collaborated in something horrible...

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:39.750
Found you!

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:48.630
Crap!

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:02.690
Damn it!

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:05.650
Why the heck are we even doing this?

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:09.200
Even if we win, the world is just going to turn against us!

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.200
In that case...

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:13.120
Why are we doing this, huh?

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:18.870
If you can't find that answer on your own, you should go to a different academy.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:22.370
Wouldn't you be happier if you went elsewhere while you still can?

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.000
Hey, everyone!

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.250
I have a super important announcement to make.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:30.170
Doesn't it look like some of you guys aren't doin' too hot at the moment?

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:35.430
So like, if I see any sticky spots, what do you say I run over to console ya?

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:39.680
Hear that? If we don't fight hard, that moron's gonna come get in our way!

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:42.190
Stay out of this!

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:45.560
You could be a national treasure the way they hate you.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.230
Dummy! They're just pretending to hate me.

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:49.030
No we're not!

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:52.240
At any rate, I determine that the situation is dire.

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:54.990
Isn't it a simple matter of needing more manpower?

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:56.870
Then we'll help you.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:58.540
Kobolds?

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:00.370
Right, Kobolds!

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:04.880
The stones Mr. Parted Hair gave us are the ore that the Kobolds live in!

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:06.880
Leave all the odd jobs to the Kobolds!

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.670
Okay, then I could use your help.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.130
Let's go.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:18.810
I, Aoi Tori, and Horizon Ariadust are right here.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:19.600
We won't run away!

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:27.110
So I'm sure there are plenty of things you can't do and things you wish you could just toss aside.

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:31.030
But for now, please leave everything that's impossible to me!

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:32.950
In exchange, I'm begging you!

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:36.240
Please tell yourselves, "I can do it!"

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:37.910
Judge!

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.240
You can believe in me, Chancellor of Musashi!

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:42.710
Everyone, line up!

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:44.420
Take your positions!

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:45.370
Judge!

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:47.880
Please fix this situation!

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:49.380
Judgment!

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:49.920
Judge!

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:50.460
Judge!

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:51.010
Judge!

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:56.840
We have already been punished by the Testament Union!

00:10:57.260 --> 00:11:01.810
We must carry the possibilities of our king and the emotions of our princess!

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:05.440
But we must never give our king or princess cause for grief!

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:07.100
You bastard! Off your high horses!

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:10.070
We bear the weight of decline!

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:13.150
We're fighting to stop our sun from setting!

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.610
We're saturated with our own downfall!

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:24.330
The empire where the sun never sets declares to the fallen nation where the sun never rises...

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:26.210
We are invincible!

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:27.210
Tres España!

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.420
Victory will be ours!

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:30.420
Tres España!

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:32.090
Glory will be ours!

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:33.130
Tres España!

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:38.260
He-na-re-s!

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:44.600
Henares! Henares! Henares!

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.350
Testament!

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:00.240
Isn't that... the British fleet?

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:06.580
Nicholas, use the great seal.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:09.250
Agree to the content included in the Far East's proposal.

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:10.500
Okay!

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.340
Save you from anything...

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:24.350
Can't the word "you" also refer to a group of people?

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:28.270
In that case, I am not breaking my promise.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:31.190
Have Howard send out the other ships!

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:31.730
Tes!

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:38.900
Go, just as we did back in our day, you group of fools...

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:01.340
<i>Now Lord Muneshige will not lose his inherited name!</i>

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:03.850
Just the shaft?

00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:06.310
You must pardon me!

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:09.480
One!

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:12.690
Two!

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:26.870
Honestly...

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:29.580
This is what happens when I do something I am unaccustomed to.

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:34.000
Honestly!

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:37.800
To think that I had to bring out armament equivalent to...

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:40.760
...what I used when I lost to Lord Muneshige.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:43.680
Its equivalent?

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:48.390
Drill, Quattro Cruz.

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:54.310
Eliminate him, commissions!

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:01.610
Butcher boy!

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:04.820
One-man hit and run!

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.160
Rolls with 10,000 coins!

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:13.960
<i>I'm running out of time!</i>

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:17.630
Old Man Velásquez, use it!

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:23.090
That's the Testament Armament's Crus Temperantia Novum.<i></i>

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:26.800
It can divide the effectiveness of my foe's move by the number of times it has been used.<i></i>

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.310
And then there's my Crus Temperantia Vetus!<i></i>

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:34.020
It doubles the enemy's cast time.<i></i>

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:38.360
Here ya go.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.450
Shit! I accidentally dumped our men with them.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:50.370
We're Musashi's relief party!

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:55.620
Go on! Spread stories of my charity to the young girls in Tres España!

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:59.170
Well, tell me what you would like to eat.

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:01.460
Fried rice, then.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.800
Okay, curry it is!

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:05.260
Fork over some fried rice!

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:06.470
All right.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.720
Here! It's fried rice.

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:11.180
That's curry!

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:15.310
You bastard! How are you going to fix this?!

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:21.480
Clerk, it's time.

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:26.450
Hey, Takakane, it's about time for our last spurt.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:28.160
Home...

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:32.620
run!

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:35.290
What?!

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.510
You're wearing money?!

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:45.550
You've lost this game!

00:15:50.430 --> 00:15:51.760
<i>He's stalling.</i>

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:55.560
<i>With the Crus Temperantia activated,
it will take twice as long for the coins to fall.</i>

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:57.060
<i>In that case!</i>

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:03.820
Swift attack!

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:07.360
Eliminate him, commissions!

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:10.990
<i>Is this the end?</i>

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:17.160
Guys!

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:19.120
Captain, keep going!

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:21.080
Keep going!

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:23.630
Tes.

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.640
Super Destructive Oscillation Cannon: Roaring Fury!

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:42.770
Wha—

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:43.610
To the right!

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:51.660
Those wings came from a God of War that crashed in Mikawa!

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:56.660
Does everyone know about Suzaku?

00:16:56.660 --> 00:17:00.370
Yeah, Naomasa decided that she was going to fight.

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:03.590
So you should cheer for her.

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:12.800
I'll cover your fees, bloodhound of England and silver wolf of Musashi!

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:18.060
Let's do this!

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:18.890
Tes.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:21.600
Bites!

00:17:25.610 --> 00:17:27.230
You're in the way!

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.110
Eat this!

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:35.530
Don't underestimate the Vice Chancellor!

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:40.460
This is my last coin! You can have it!

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:00.600
Game, set, match.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:15.450
How could I throw the game when I'm the Vice Chancellor?!

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:16.780
It's not over yet!

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:20.160
Tres España isn't done yet!

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:32.760
Captain!

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:36.680
The game's over!

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:38.640
Damn it!

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:44.810
Hit her, Jizuri Suzaku!

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:51.780
Lunge into her, Jizuri Suzaku!

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:56.240
Pathfinder Byakko, draw her in!

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:13.090
Now you're—

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:19.260
That's my little sister.

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:24.600
When our village got attacked, Jizuri Suzaku still couldn't move.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:28.310
That's when my sister told me.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.070
Even though she wasn't breathing anymore,

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:33.610
she said to "use me".

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:37.950
So... I will use her!

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:39.450
I will!

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:43.160
Get up, Jizuri Suzaku!

00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:46.160
Stop her, Pathfinder Byakko!

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:52.960
<i>What?</i>

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:00.800
<i>A Sacred God...?</i>

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:02.100
<i>It can't be!</i>

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:04.810
<i>Does this mean Suzaku came out to protect her?</i>

00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:13.320
Water? No, this is... the sky?!

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:46.520
<i>How did Lord Muneshige best this foe?</i>

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:50.190
Bind, Slicing Dragonfly!

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:12.580
<i>Arcabuz Cruz is a massive siege armament.</i>

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.710
<i>And her hands wield dual swords.</i>

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:16.590
<i>What wonderful matrimonial love!</i>

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:45.410
Arcabuz Cruz!

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:47.740
Bind, Slicing Dragonfly!

00:21:57.710 --> 00:21:58.670
One!

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:07.310
Two!

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:25.780
<i>This is bad...</i>

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:30.410
<i>At this rate, I will begin comparing this woman to Master Muneshige.</i>

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:41.010
I have...

00:22:44.260 --> 00:22:45.800
I have lost.

00:22:54.190 --> 00:22:57.860
The enemy leader, Tachibana Gin, is down!

00:24:04.050 --> 00:24:05.470
<i>Master Muneshige...</i>
